# Ask / moments (frontend)

Read [`docs/api-frontend.md`](../../docs/api-frontend.md) § Ask / moments. Call the API **only** through [`apps/web/app/lib/api.ts`](../../apps/web/app/lib/api.ts) with `credentials: 'include'`. Never send `Authorization: Bearer`.

Reference UI: [`moment-search.tsx`](../../apps/web/app/components/summary/moment-search.tsx) (`AskMint` continuous thread in the right editor pane — default **Ask Mint** tab; no modal. Append turns on each ask; composer stays available). Clip export: [`use-moment-clip-export.ts`](../../apps/web/app/hooks/use-moment-clip-export.ts).

The **backend** classifies intent. Do **not** regex-detect question vs clip on the client.

## One box → `api.askMoments(recordingId, { query })`

`POST /api/recordings/:id/moments/ask`

```json
{ "query": "What did they say about pricing?", "limit": 8 }
```

- `id` / `recordingId` are **integers** (recording, not project).
- `query`: trimmed string, **3–500** chars. Optional `limit` (default 8, max 50) only affects clip hits.
- Cookie session required → `401` if missing.

Use this for the recording editor ask/search input. Prefer `askMoments` over `searchMoments` unless you only want clip vectors (no Q&A / reject).

## Switch on `kind`

```ts
type AskMomentsResponse =
  | { kind: 'answer'; text: string }
  | { kind: 'moments'; moments: MomentCandidate[] }
  | { kind: 'reject'; text: string };
```

| `kind` | When | UI |
|---|---|---|
| `answer` | Transcript question | Render `text` (no clip cards) |
| `moments` | Find / cut a moment | Cards + preview seek + **Cut clip** |
| `reject` | Off-topic | Render `text` as a light/funny refusal — do not toast as an error |

`moments: []` with `kind: 'moments'` → empty state (“No matching moments”), not a reject.

### Moment card fields (ms)

```json
{
  "startMs": 12000,
  "endMs": 42000,
  "clipStartMs": 9000,
  "clipEndMs": 47000,
  "title": "The enterprise plan starts at",
  "excerpt": "We should talk about pricing…",
  "similarity": 0.82
}
```

- Preview / seek: `seek(startMs / 1000)` (player is **seconds**).
- Labels: format `startMs` / `endMs` in the UI.
- **Cut clip** must send **padded** bounds: `clipStartMs` / `clipEndMs`, not `startMs` / `endMs`.
- `similarity` is 0..1 — show as a friendly match badge (e.g. `82% match`), not a raw `0.82`. Tooltip should be ELI5 (no cosine/jargon): Mint compared your ask to this video bit; closer to 100% is a better fit. `title` / `excerpt` are display-only.

## Cut clip — `api.createClip`

`POST /api/clips` (201). `hookId` omitted / null.

```json
{
  "recordingId": 10,
  "title": "The enterprise plan starts at",
  "startMs": 9000,
  "endMs": 47000,
  "aspectRatio": "9:16",
  "fitMode": "fit",
  "burnSubtitles": true
}
```

`aspectRatio` defaults to the player chip (`9:16` / `1:1` / `16:9`); confirm dialog can override before cut. `fitMode` defaults `fit` (Keep full frame + blur); `fill` is opt-in center crop. `burnSubtitles` defaults `true`.

Then poll `GET /api/clips/:id` (`api.getClip`) every **2–5s** while `status` is `queued` | `rendering`. Stop on `ready` | `failed`. Download `videoUrl` (HTTPS Filestack only). Same pattern as hook export (`useHookClipExport` / `useMomentClipExport`).

Errors: `404` not owned, `400 INVALID_CLIP_RANGE`, `409 VIDEO_NOT_AVAILABLE`.

AI hook **Cut clip** stays `api.exportHookClip(recordingId, hookId)` — do not mix the two.

## Errors (`{ "error": "…" }`)

| Status | `error` | UI |
|---|---|---|
| `400` | validation | Query too short / invalid |
| `401` | `UNAUTHORIZED` | Send to login |
| `404` | `Not found` | Recording missing / not owned |
| `409` | `TRANSCRIPT_REQUIRED` | “Transcript is not ready yet.” |
| `409` | `TRANSCRIPT_INDEX_NOT_READY` | “Re-run processing to index this transcript.” (`POST /recordings/:id/retry`) |
| `409` | `VIDEO_NOT_AVAILABLE` | On clip create only |

Do not show stack traces. `kind: 'reject'` is **200**, not an error.

## Do not

- Classify intent in the browser.
- Call Qdrant, OpenAI, or PyAI from the web app.
- Persist ask results into the `hooks` list (regenerate-hooks would wipe them).
- Use `searchMoments` for the ask box (no Q&A / reject).
- Send `startMs`/`endMs` when cutting an ask-hit — use `clipStartMs`/`clipEndMs`.
